title: Aryan_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Angry_1>>
<<SetBGSprite WellingtonEstate>>

Despite knowing the discomfort it brings, Raju accompanies his mother to the high-rise complex today, carrying her work basket.

The gleaming marble floors mock Raju's worn sandals.

The air smells of expensive cleaning products and privilege.

Each step reminds him of the social hierarchy here. He knows confrontations are inevitable in this gilded world.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: Oh, look who's back.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: The servant boy returns.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: What's the matter, slum boy?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: Did you lose your way to the garbage dump again?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Angry">>
Raju: I'm not your servant.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Angry">>
Raju: I'm here to help my mother, that's all.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: Help? Oh, that's rich!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: Your mother cleans our toilets, and you carry her bags.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: Very inspiring.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: I bet you think you're special because you kick a ball around in the dirt.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: But that's not real cricket, you know.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: You probably can't even hold a bat properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Angry">>
Raju: I can play cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Angry">>
Raju: Better than you think.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Angry">>
Raju: Better than you, probably.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Excited">>
Aryan: Better than me? Ha!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: That's the funniest thing I've heard all week.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: You with your bare feet and torn clothes?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: You think you can beat someone with real coaching?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Tell you what, slum boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: If you're so confident, come back tomorrow.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Bring whatever pathetic excuse for cricket equipment you have.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: We'll see just how good you really are.

<<HideCharacter>>

Aryan's mocking laughter echoes as Raju walks away. His hands clench into fists.

A fire of determination burns away the initial sting of humiliation.

Tomorrow will be about much more than cricket. It's a clash between two worlds.

<<set $Aryan_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===
title: Aryan_Day2
tags: 
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Angry_1>>
<<SetBGSprite WellingtonEstate>>

After last confrontation with Aryan, Raju returns to the high-rise complex today.

He carries his simple cricket bat, its worn handle standing in stark contrast to the polished marble around him.

His heart pounds as he spots Aryan near the fountain, casually handling professional-grade cricket equipment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: Well, well. The slum boy returns.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: And look what I have here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: Genuine English willow, imported directly from the finest manufacturers.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: I bet you've never even touched something this valuable, have you?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: It's a beautiful bat.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: But it's still just a piece of willow wood.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: The bat doesn't hit the boundaries - the batsman does.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: That's exactly what losers say!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: They make themselves feel better about having inferior equipment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: When you have proper coaching and professional equipment, natural talent becomes irrelevant.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: You think you can play cricket with your makeshift bats and tennis balls?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: That's not real cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: That's just poor kids playing in the dirt and pretending it matters.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: You want to see what I can do?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Fine. I'll show you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Cricket isn't about how much money your family has.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Excited">>
Aryan: Oh, this is perfect!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Excited">>
Aryan: The confident little slum boy thinks he can actually compete.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Excited">>
Aryan: This will be entertaining.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Tomorrow afternoon, right here in this courtyard.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: A proper cricket challenge.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: You with your pathetic equipment against me with my professional gear.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: My friends will be here to watch.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I'll be here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: And when it's over, you'll understand something important.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Respect isn't something money can buy.

<<HideCharacter>>

As Raju departs the complex, he feels the weight of what he has committed to.

Not just a game of cricket, but a public test of everything he believes.

The anticipation mixes with anxiety. Failure tomorrow would validate every cruel assumption about his background.

<<set $Aryan_Day = 3>>
<<EndEvent true>>
