<<PlayBackgroundMusic Angry_1>>
<<SetBGSprite WellingtonEstate>>

Knowing that upcoming challenge with Aryan will be witnessed by his friends, Raju visits the complex again today.

The complex buzzes with excitement. Word of the cricket challenge has spread among the wealthy children.

Raju can feel their curious and dismissive glances as he moves through the corridors.

This match has become a symbol of class conflict and social hierarchy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Excited">>
Jaspreet: I can't believe you actually challenged that slum boy to cricket!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: What if he turns out to be actually good at it?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: I mean, some of those street kids are surprisingly athletic.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: Good? Please, Jaspreet.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: He probably learned cricket by playing with rocks and sticks in garbage dumps.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Smiling">>
Aryan: There's a difference between street games and real cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: But Aryan, I heard some kids from the regular school saying he's actually not bad.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: What if you're underestimating him?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: It doesn't matter if he has some natural ability.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: When you have proper equipment, professional coaching, and dedicated practice facilities...

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Raw talent becomes meaningless.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Excited">>
Aryan: Oh look, everyone! The challenger arrives!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Excited">>
Aryan: Perfect timing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Excited">>
Aryan: I was just telling my friends about tomorrow's entertainment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Are you ready for your public humiliation, slum boy?
