title: Aryan_Day5
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Angry_1>>
<<SetBGSprite WellingtonEstate>>

The moment of truth has arrived.

Despite his nerves, Raju meets Aryan at the high-rise complex for their cricket challenge.

The courtyard has been transformed into an arena of judgment.

Curious residents gather to witness the culmination of days of building tension.

The air vibrates with anticipation and barely concealed prejudice as Raju arrives.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Excited">>
Jaspreet: Finally! The main event!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Excited">>
Jaspreet: Go on, Aryan!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Excited">>
Jaspreet: Show this slum boy how real cricket is played!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Watch carefully, everyone.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: This is what happens when street pretenders face real cricketers.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: Let's see you even touch this ball, slum boy!

// The first delivery comes fast and precise, but Raju watches with intense focus. The connection is sweet and pure - bat meeting ball with a satisfying crack.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: Ooooooh! Did you see that shot?!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: That went straight to the boundary!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Angry">>
Aryan: That was just a lucky shot!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" Angry>>
Aryan: Anyone can get lucky once!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" Angry>>
Aryan: Try again - let's see if you can do it twice!

<<HideCharacter>>
The second delivery produces another clean strike that sends the ball soaring.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: That... that was actually a really good shot.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Jaspreet" "Quizzical">>
Jaspreet: How did he read that delivery so well?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Quizzical">>
Aryan: I... I don't understand.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Quizzical">>
Aryan: He's playing like someone who's been properly trained.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Quizzical">>
Aryan: But that's impossible.

<<HideCharacter>>
The third delivery reveals the full extent of Raju's skill - placed with surgical precision.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: ...Not bad, slum boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Not bad at all.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: But don't think this changes anything between us.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I told you cricket isn't about equipment or social class.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: It's about dedication, practice, and love for the game.

<<HideCharacter>>

The crowd disperses in stunned silence.

Their preconceptions shattered by Raju's unexpected display of genuine cricket mastery.

The young man from the slums stands quietly in the center of the courtyard.

The moment represents more than athletic victory - it is a fundamental challenge to assumptions about wealth and worth.

<<set $Aryan_Day = 6>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===
title: Aryan_Day6
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Angry_1>>
<<SetBGSprite WellingtonEstate>>

After his surprising cricket performance, Raju returns to the high-rise complex one final time.

The atmosphere in the complex has shifted dramatically.

The smugness and casual cruelty of privilege have been replaced by uncomfortable recognition.

Talent and worth cannot be purchased or inherited.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Sad">>
Aryan: I still can't believe it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Sad">>
Aryan: You actually beat me.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Sad">>
Aryan: Not just once, but consistently, shot after shot.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Sad">>
Aryan: My friends haven't stopped talking about it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I tried to tell you from the beginning.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Cricket isn't about expensive bats or fancy shoes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: It's about heart, dedication, and genuine love for the game.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Quizzical">>
Aryan: Maybe... maybe you're right about some things.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Quizzical">>
Aryan: You do have something I didn't expect.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Quizzical">>
Aryan: Something raw, natural, authentic.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: But don't think your performance changes everything between us.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: You may have beaten me at cricket, but that doesn't erase our fundamental differences.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: I never expected it to change our social positions, Aryan.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: I just wanted you to understand something.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Talent and worth aren't distributed according to wealth.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Respect... yes, I suppose you've earned that.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: This won't be the last time we compete.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: I'll get better, train harder, and one day I will beat you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Then I'll be ready.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: And I'll keep getting better too.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Smiling">>
Raju: Having a real competitor will make us both stronger players.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: ...You're not bad, slum boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: Not bad at all.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" "Serious">>
Aryan: But next time will be different.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I'm looking forward to it.

<<HideCharacter>>

As Raju leaves the complex for what may be the final time, he carries satisfaction with him.

He has challenged and changed entrenched assumptions about class, worth, and capability.

His victory over Aryan represents more than personal triumph.

It stands as proof that dignity, skill, and character cannot be purchased, inherited, or taken away by those who mistake privilege for superiority.

<<set $Aryan_Complete = true>>
<<jump Courage>>
